{
  "_help": [
    "PLOT PRESETS and DASHBOARD VIEWS for OG1 gliders and ALRs (the og1 platform, platforms/og1.py). Each platform has its own file like this one; the app name and colour palettes are shared, in glider_playground/plot_presets.json. Read by the backend (startup pre-caching) and by every page (served as /api/plot_presets.js). Restart the app after editing.",
    "ADD A PRESET: copy a block in 'presets', give it a new key (preset_<something>), and edit it. It appears as a toolbar button automatically, greyed out for files that lack its variables.",
    "  label      - button text.",
    "  icon       - a Material Symbols icon name (fonts.google.com/icons).",
    "  colour     - button colour: red, purple, blue, indigo, green, cyan, amber, yellow, gray - or any hex like '#e879f9'.",
    "  x / y / c  - variable names to try IN ORDER; the first one present in the file wins (its _ADJUSTED variant is preferred automatically). Either a list, or the name of a shared list from 'axes' (e.g. 'time', 'depth').",
    "  cmap       - a name from 'palettes' (append _r to reverse it), or 'discrete_09' for integer flags, or 'black'.",
    "  invert_y   - true for depth/pressure on the y axis.",
    "  draw_order - optional: normal | outliers | smallest | largest (which points are drawn on top).",
    "  prewarm    - true = pre-cache this plot when a file is first processed, so the first click is instant. Only applies to files processed after the change.",
    "  group      - optional: presets sharing a group name fold into one toolbar chip that opens a menu on hover (the chip shows whichever member is active). Presets without a group stay as their own chip.",
    "  points     - optional, with lines: true draws each variable as points instead of connected lines.",
    "  requires   - optional: variables that must ALL be in the file, otherwise the preset is hidden rather than greyed out (e.g. a second sensor).",
    "  c: []      - no colour variable: points are drawn in one colour (use cmap 'black').",
    "  lines      - optional: several variables drawn as connected lines against x on ONE plot (e.g. Dive). Each entry is a variable name, a candidate list, or a shared list from 'axes'; variables the file lacks are skipped. Variables with the same units share an axis: the first unit on the left (inverted if invert_y), the second on the right.",
    "VIEWS: which presets each built-in view shows, in order. Presets the file can't satisfy are skipped. An entry is a preset key, or {\"preset\": key, \"draw_order\": ...} to override. 'duo' uses exactly two. 'new_plot_order' is the preference order when adding a new plot panel. 'invert_y_vars' are y variables that auto-switch Invert-Y on when picked by hand."
  ],
